WEBVTT - Echoes of the Deep: Field Audio Recording
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00.000 --> 00:03.500
[Pacific tide swell rolling across rocky shelf]
Narrator: Chapter One: Sound in the Abyss.

00:03.500 --> 00:07.800
[Subtle hydrophone ping and deep underwater current resonance]
Dr. Elena Rostova: When you close your eyes, the Pacific ocean isn't silent at all. It's an orchestral symphony of seismic rumbles and marine life.

00:07.800 --> 00:11.200
[Echolocation click train accelerated]
Marcus Thorne: We have detected a pod of Cuvier’s beaked whales diving beneath 2,500 meters.

00:11.200 --> 00:15.500
[Resonant bass harmonic drone]
Dr. Elena Rostova: Every click serves as their flashlight in absolute darkness. Sound is their sensory sight.
